"Counting-by-key benchmark (dict, design note
docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-12-dict-design.md §10 item 3). Stone
counting with public rules: a 0 becomes 1; a number with an even count of
digits splits into its two halves; any other number is multiplied by
2024. Eight synthetic starting stones, 75 blinks. Each blink rebuilds a
dict of counts keyed by stone with `dict.update-strict`, so the counts
(about 3.2e14 in total, 3634 distinct stones at the end) stay exact and
no chain of unevaluated additions builds up.

Expected total computed independently (Python, collections.Counter)."

` "the number of decimal digits of `n`"
digits(n): (n < 10) then(1, 1 + digits(n / 10))

` "ten to the power `k`"
pow10(k): (k = 0) then(1, 10 * pow10(k - 1))

` "the halves of `n`, which has `d` digits (an even number)"
halves(n, d): { p: pow10(d / 2) }.[n / p, n % p]

` "the stones one stone `s` becomes after a blink"
children(s): { d: digits(s) }.(cond[s = 0 => [1], d % 2 = 0 => halves(s, d), [s * 2024]])

` "add `n` stones `c` to the counts `acc`"
add(n, acc, c): acc dict.update-strict(c, + n, 0)

` "add the children of the `n` stones `s` to the counts `acc`"
spawn(acc, [s, n]): s children foldl(add(n), acc)

` "the counts after one blink"
blink(counts): counts dict.to-list foldl(spawn, dict.empty)

` "the counts after `k` blinks"
blinks(k, counts): (k = 0) then(counts, blinks(k - 1, counts blink))

` "one stone `s`, as a `[stone, count]` entry"
one(s): [s, 1]

` :suppress
start: [0, 7, 125, 17, 4048, 9999, 802, 31415926] map(one) dict.of

` :suppress
final: blinks(75, start)

` { target: :bench-dict-counting
    verify: ["default-expectation"] }
bench-dict-counting: {
  total: final dict.values sum
  distinct: final dict.size
  RESULT: (total = 315290635574411 ∧ distinct = 3634) then(:PASS, :FAIL)
}
